nipc - u get stable result\n\nUse 576p resolution and 81 length and set 16 frame_rate on Video Combine to get the best results\nAlso u can generate with 121 length and set 24 frame_rate, but u may get more less stable result\n\nIn 720p (1280x720) 10 steps u can get more beautiful picture\n\nuse CFG 1.0 to get faster generation or use CFG 2.0 to get more cool result, but generation takes more time if cfg>1. With CFG 2.0 u necessarily write negative prompt (cfg 1 doesn't reqiuere negative prompt)\n\nRecomended resolution: 576x1024, 1024x576, 1280x720, 720x1280\n\nHow to set length (frames) correctly:\n\nfor 16 fps\n16 * number of seconds = length and set frame_rate 16 on Video Combine\n\nfor 24 fps\n24 * number of seconds = length and set frame_rate 24 on Video Combine\n\nI don't recommend generate videos more than 5 seconds because your generation will be unstable and the picture won't be good\n\nI recomend leave 8 steps with 4steps loras, but u can try set 10 steps - you may get better result\n\nIf u want generate more dynamic video with minimum artefacts, turn off lightx loras, set 20 steps in 480p or 30 steps in 720p, cfg from 3.5 to 5 to each ksampler \n\nTry adjusting WanVideoBlockSwap settings\n\nMy results with rtx 5080 generation\n\nWith 4steps loras\n576p, light Lora 250928, 81 length (16 fps), 10 steps, unipc, cfg 2.0 (high noise only) ≈ 5-6 minutes\n720p, light Lora 250928, 81 length (16 fps), 10 steps, unipc, cfg 2.0 (high noise only) ≈ 10-11 minutes\n576p, light Lora 250928, 129 length (16 fps), 10 steps, res2m_ode, cfg 2.0 (high noise only) ≈ 12 minutes\n720p, light Lora 250928, 129 length (16 fps), 10 steps, unipc, cfg 2.0 (high noise only) ≈ 15-16 minutes\n\nWithout LightX\n480p, 81 length (16 fps), 20 steps, unipc, cfg 3.5 ≈ 10 minutes\n720p, 81 length (16 fps), 30 steps, unipc, cfg 3.5 ≈ 35 minutes\n\n\n"],"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":91,"type":"UnetLoaderGGUFDisTorch2MultiGPU","pos":[190.698782129672,297.6251318070183],"size":[335.6441406